{"learnerLanguage":"es","spokenSeconds":150,"turns":[{"speaker":"character","text":"Good morning. My name is Anna. What's your full name?"},{"speaker":"learner","text":"Good morning. My name is Javier Martín."},{"speaker":"character","text":"Let's talk about free time. What do you like to do at the weekend?"},{"speaker":"learner","text":"At the weekend I usually go to the mountains with my friends, because I like very much the nature. Also I play football on Sundays."},{"speaker":"character","text":"Did you do the same things when you were a child?"},{"speaker":"learner","text":"Not exactly. When I was a child I lived in the city centre, so I played more in the street with my neighbours. We didn't go to the mountains because my parents was working a lot."},{"speaker":"character","text":"Describe a trip you enjoyed. Say where you went, who you went with, what you did, and explain why you enjoyed it."},{"speaker":"learner","text":"OK, I will talk about a trip to Lisbon two years ago. I went with my girlfriend in the summer. We visited the old part of the city, Alfama, and we eat a lot of fish and pastries. Also we took the famous tram, the number 28, but it was very full of tourists. I enjoyed it because the city is very beautiful and the people was very kind, and it was not expensive like other capitals. I would like to return in the future."},{"speaker":"character","text":"Why do people like to travel abroad?"},{"speaker":"learner","text":"I think people travel for know other cultures and for relax. When you are in other country you forget the problems of the work. But it depends of the person, some people prefer stay at home."},{"speaker":"character","text":"Do you think tourism can cause problems for cities?"},{"speaker":"learner","text":"Yes, I think so. For example in Barcelona there are too much tourists and the prices of the flats is very high for the local people. The government should to control it."}],"criteria":[{"halfBands":true,"maxBand":9,"minBand":0,"key":"fluencyCoherence","levelBand":null,"name":"Fluency and Coherence","scope":"task","sound":false,"voiceOnly":false},{"halfBands":true,"maxBand":9,"minBand":0,"key":"lexicalResource","levelBand":null,"name":"Lexical Resource","scope":"task","sound":false,"voiceOnly":false},{"halfBands":true,"maxBand":9,"minBand":0,"key":"grammar","levelBand":null,"name":"Grammatical Range and Accuracy","scope":"task","sound":false,"voiceOnly":false},{"halfBands":true,"maxBand":9,"minBand":0,"key":"pronunciation","levelBand":null,"name":"Pronunciation","scope":"task","sound":true,"voiceOnly":true}],"task":{"brief":"The test's three parts in a shorter call","minutes":{"max":5,"min":5},"name":"Speaking mock","role":"examiner"},"title":"IELTS Speaking","exam":"ielts"}